      "widgets_values": [
        "integrated_multimodal_description:\nA single continuous cinematic shot with no cuts.\n\nAt the beginning, [DESCRIBE KEYFRAME 1 / STARTING SUBJECT AND ENVIRONMENT].\n\nAs the shot progresses, [DESCRIBE THE FIRST TRANSFORMATION OR ACTION LEADING TOWARD KEYFRAME 2]. Keep the subject visually continuous and preserve its screen position, approximate scale, and identity during the transition.\n\nAround the midpoint, [DESCRIBE KEYFRAME 2 / MIDDLE STATE].\n\nDuring the second half, [DESCRIBE THE SECOND TRANSFORMATION OR ACTION LEADING TOWARD KEYFRAME 3]. The change should happen progressively rather than as a sudden replacement.\n\nBy the final moments, [DESCRIBE KEYFRAME 3 / FINAL STATE].\n\nCamera:\n[DESCRIBE ONE SIMPLE CONTINUOUS CAMERA MOVE, for example: a slow push-in with a subtle clockwise orbit]. Keep the movement smooth and coherent throughout the entire shot.\n\nContinuity:\nNo cuts, no teleportation, no sudden subject replacement, and no extra characters unless explicitly requested. The progression should read clearly as:\n[KEYFRAME 1] -> [KEYFRAME 2] -> [KEYFRAME 3].\n\noverall_soundscape:\n[DESCRIBE THE DIEGETIC AMBIENCE AND HOW IT EVOLVES THROUGH THE TRANSFORMATION].\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A\n",
